      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For posterity (and if needed) I isolated a repro for the main issue\n\nAssignSceneNetworkIDs reporting a failure\n\nRepro Steps:\n\n- Basic scene with VRCWorld Prefab\n\n- Make a prefab with a synced component on it (eg: VRCObjectSync)\n\n- Duplicate prefab\n\n- Build to assign the network IDs\n\n- Back in scene, open the prefab in prefab edit mode, remove a synced script component and add a new synced script (eg: replace VRCObjectSync with SmartObjectSync by MMMaellon) (effectively trying to trigger the \"Network Components Changed\" bit from the Network ID Utility)\n\n- Save prefab, go back to scene and attempt to build again.\n\n- The error will pop up (first pic of OP)\n\n- Go to the network IDs utility and see that the object is flagged as having network components changed, with the network IDs being the exact same.\n\n- Click Select on the items highlighted, then you can go back an build successfully.\n\nThis may be considered expected behaviour for the sake of diffing between PC and Android, but it does cause confusion when such a thing happens and prevents the build entirely from completing.\n\nLooking forward to what the Future Release might have for this.\n\nVideo of repro: https://streamable.com/kv8oi8",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
